  <FFF_RimIgnore_Template># .rimignore — files and folders to exclude when uploading to the Steam Workshop
#
# The syntax is identical to GitHub's .gitignore:
# # comment (\# for a literal hash)
# !xxx re-include; later rules override earlier ones
# /xxx anchored to the mod root
# xxx/ directories only
# * any characters, but never across /
# ? a single character, but never across /
# [abc] character set; [!abc] to negate
# **/xxx at any depth; xxx/** for everything inside that folder
#
# Note: as in Git, once a directory is excluded its contents cannot be
# re-included with !.
# Always excluded by default: this file, .git/ .gitignore .gitattributes
# .svn/ .hg/ .vs/ .idea/ .vscode/
# Thumbs.db desktop.ini .DS_Store
# Those built-in rules can be overridden with !, e.g. !.rimignore uploads this file too.

# -- Source code and build output --
/_Sources/
/Source/
**/obj/
**/bin/
*.pdb
*.csproj.user
*.sln
*.suo

# -- Unity project --
/UnityProject/

# -- Dev tools and shortcuts --
/_Tools/
*.lnk
*.bat

# -- Editor and backup noise --
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak
*~

# -- Example: exclude a folder's contents but keep one file --
# Exclude the *contents* rather than the folder itself, then re-include:
# /Docs/*
# !/Docs/Manual.md</FFF_RimIgnore_Template>
